 "standard_url": "https://www.education.gov.za/Portals/0/CD/National%20Curriculum%20Statements%20and%20Vocational/CAPS%20SP%20%20MATHEMATICS%20GR%207-9.pdf",
 "standard_text": "Recognise and interpret rules or relationships represented in symbolic form; identify variables and constants in given formulae and/or equations; recognise and identify like and unlike terms; add and subtract like terms; use substitution to determine the value of an expression.",
 "meta_desc": "Free CAPS Grade 7 algebraic expressions worksheets: notation, writing expressions, like terms, simplifying and substitution. 100 questions with memos.",
 "key_big": "3x means 3 × x.",
 "key_sub": "Only add like terms.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>3x means 3 × x. x² means x × x. <span class='fr'><span class='fn'>x</span><span class='fd'>4</span></span> means x ÷ 4.</li><li>Like terms have the same letter part: 5a + 2a = 7a, but 5a + 2b cannot be simplified.</li><li>Substitution: put the number in place of the letter and use the order of operations.</li><li>If a = 4, then 3a + 5 = 3 × 4 + 5 = 17.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Simplify 4x + 7 − x + 2</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>4x − x = 3x</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>7 + 2 = 9</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 3x + 9</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3x as x + 3</td><td>3x = 3 × x.</td></tr><tr><td>Unlike terms</td><td>Only add terms with the same letters.</td></tr><tr><td>Order of operations</td><td>Multiply before you add.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
